  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1028 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge over the southeastern CONUS will begin to \nshift back westward beginning on Wednesday. This will effectively \nreturn us to convective chances closer to the Texas/New Mexico state \nline on Wednesday and Thursday. By late in the week, the retreating \nridge will significantly weaken with increasing troughing over the \nsouthwestern CONUS. A number of short wave troughs within the \nsouthwest flow may bring periodic rain chances this weekend through \nearly next week. The increased chances of rainfall and a possible \ncold front this weekend will bring much lower temperatures back to \nmore seasonal values.",
